From 9cd8d1b03e6544f3d1040e08b5a9833731164c9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott <158021536+nathawatc@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:07:30 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(build): fail configure on unresolvable pkg-config
 Requires (#16)

## What

- Add `howdy_pkg_check_modules()` (`cmake/howdy_pkg_config.cmake`) and
use it for all pkg-config dependencies instead of `pkg_check_modules()`.
- Before the lookup it runs the same `pkg-config --cflags --libs` query,
using FindPkgConfig's `CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH` search paths, and fails
configure if that query fails.
- It re-queries once per build tree, so results that an unpatched CMake
4.5 configure cached with empty flags are replaced.

## Why

Since CMake 4.5 (!12204), `pkg_check_modules(REQUIRED)` uses
`--modversion`, which pkgconf answers without resolving `Requires`. It
also ignores failing `--cflags`/`--libs` queries, so a package with a
missing dependency is reported as found with empty flags.
`native-cross-pkg-config-isolation` fails on CMake 4.5.0 because of
this.

It's unclear whether CMake intends this, so we carry the check
ourselves. See #15.

## Tests

- New native cases: missing `Requires`, resolved `Requires`, packages
found only through `CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH`, reconfigure after a failure, and
a build tree cached before this change.
- Expected-failure cases now check their error message.
- The harness passes every per-run setting on every run. Previously a
seeded `-D` value stayed in the build cache, so the second
`stale-cache-isolation` configure never ran its checks.

Results:
- CMake 4.5.0 on the host: 109/109
- Arch CI (CMake 4.4.5): 109/109
- Nix CI (freedesktop.org pkg-config 0.29.2): 108/108

Refs #15
